From: mscharged-port
Subject: Select fog and vertex array byte order per draw
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

The fog type, fog range adjustment and each vertex array's byte order were
part of the shader configuration, so the same draw state needed a separate
pipeline for every fog type a stadium uses and for each byte order of its
arrays. A pipeline catalogue had to list every one of these variants, and an
effect first seen under another stadium's fog compiled while drawing.

They are now per-draw state in DrawImmediateData::drawFlags (the spare
immediate word): bits 0-11 mark little-endian arrays, bits 16-19 hold the
fog type and bit 20 enables range adjustment. Every shader carries the fog
uniforms and selects the original fog equation at runtime; vertex fetches
pass the byte order bit to the existing fetch helpers, which already took it
as a runtime argument. An invalid fog type still stops at the draw. The
shader configuration keeps its layout with the former fields reserved (zero),
and GXPipelineConfigVersion becomes 17, so earlier cache records are not
loaded. Fog type and range changes no longer invalidate the pipeline.

